title: The Siege of Havana
tags: event
view-if: war_stage = 3

= Approaching Havana

The American army marches steadily west from Matanzas, its supply trains stretching for miles behind the advancing columns. Villages liberated by the Mambises greet the expedition as it passes, while fleeing Spanish detachments fall back toward the island's capital. Every road now leads to Havana, the political and military heart of Spanish Cuba.

Beyond its ancient walls and formidable forts lies the strongest concentration of Spanish troops remaining on the island. Morro Castle commands the harbor, batteries guard every approach, and seasoned regulars prepare to defend the city street by street if necessary. Yet Spain's position grows weaker with every passing day. Mambise guerrillas continue to harass communications across the countryside, while the Carlist War and the Cantonal Rebellion consume Madrid's attention and leave few reinforcements available for Cuba.

The fate of the campaign will be decided before the walls of Havana.

- @Advance: Advance on Havana.
- @Withdraw: Halt the advance.

@Advance
subtitle: Commit to taking the city.
on-arrival: {!

let effective_garrison = Math.max(Q.spain_havana_garrison_strength - (Q.mambise_strength * 0.5), 60);
let american_strength = Q.invasion_force_strength + (Q.navy_strength * 0.05);

Q.havana_siege_duration = 0;

if (american_strength >= effective_garrison * 1.3) {
Q.havana_outcome = "decisive_win";
} else {
Q.havana_outcome = "siege";
Q.havana_garrison_remaining = effective_garrison;
}
Q.war_stage = 4;

!}
go-to: Decisive_Win if havana_outcome = "decisive_win"; Siege_Begins if havana_outcome = "siege"

@Withdraw
subtitle: Call off the advance on Havana.
on-arrival: spain_war = 0
go-to: Defeat

@Decisive_Win

= Decisive Win

News of the American advance reaches Havana well before the army itself. Reports of shattered coastal defenses, the loss of Matanzas, and relentless Mambise activity convince the Spanish commander that no meaningful relief force will arrive. With morale collapsing and supplies dwindling, the prospect of resisting a superior American army appears hopeless.

Rather than endure a prolonged bombardment, the city's defenses begin to unravel. American troops occupy the outer fortifications with only scattered resistance, and within days the Stars and Stripes rises above Morro Castle as Spanish forces lay down their arms. What many feared would become a bloody siege instead ends in a remarkably swift victory.

- @Continue: Continue

@Continue
on-arrival: spain_surrendered = 1; spain_war = 0

With Havana in American hands, organized Spanish resistance on Cuba effectively comes to an end. Deprived of its colonial capital and unable to reinforce the island, Madrid has little choice but to seek peace. Diplomatic messages are dispatched through European intermediaries requesting negotiations to end the war.

@Siege_Begins

= Americans Dig In

The defenders refuse to yield.

Spanish engineers reinforce barricades throughout the city while artillery crews prepare for a lengthy siege. From the walls of Morro Castle, heavy guns answer every American battery brought into position, filling the harbor with smoke and thunder. Attempts to probe the defenses are driven back by determined volleys, making it clear that Havana will not fall in a single assault.

American soldiers settle into trenches surrounding the city as engineers construct siege works and supply depots. Beyond the lines, Mambise fighters continue to raid Spanish communications in the hope of preventing reinforcements from reaching the capital. Whether Havana ultimately falls through starvation and bombardment or is saved by a desperate relief effort from the south now depends on which side can endure longer.

- @Continue_Siege: Continue

@Continue_Siege
go-to: Havana_Siege_Resolution

The siege settles into an exhausting routine of trenches, bombardments, and constant skirmishing. Every passing week brings the defenders closer to exhaustion, but each delay also grants Spain another opportunity to gather whatever forces it can and attempt one final effort to save Havana.